From: Pyra kernel work <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: pyra v5.2/v5.3: make the jack-detect line an input

The TS3A227E headset detector signals on line 14 of the PCAL6524
expander (P16, "mic-int"). On a V5.3 unit that line reaches the kernel
configured as an output: bank 1's configuration register reads 0x08
straight after boot. gpiolib caches that direction when the expander is
added, and because the expander sleeps it never re-reads it, so the
TS3A227E's interrupt request fails on every boot:

  gpio gpiochip10: (4-0022): gpiochip_lock_as_irq: tried to flag a GPIO set as output for IRQ
  ts3a227e 4-003b: Cannot request irq 197 (-5)
  ts3a227e: probe of 4-003b failed with error -5

Hog the line as an input. Hogs are applied in of_gpiochip_add(), before
gpiochip_add_data() reads back each line's direction, so the register
and the cached flag both say input by the time the TS3A227E probes.

Set to input by hand on a running system, the TS3A227E binds and tracks
the jack: accessory status 0x00 empty, 0x09 with 3-pole headphones, one
interrupt per plug and unplug.

Only the two board files that give the TS3A227E an interrupt change.
The sound card still takes its jack state from the TWL6040; this only
lets the detector probe.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/pyra-mainboard-v5.2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/pyra-mainboard-v5.2.dtsi
@@ -54,6 +54,19 @@
 	compatible = "nxp,pcal6524";
 	interrupt-parent = <&gpio6>;
 	interrupts = <1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;	/* gpio6_161 */
+
+	/*
+	 * The TS3A227E's interrupt (P16). It reaches the kernel configured
+	 * as an output, so gpiolib refuses it as an IRQ and the jack
+	 * detector fails to probe with -EIO. Make it an input before
+	 * anything asks for it.
+	 */
+	mic-int-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <14 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		input;
+		line-name = "mic-int";
+	};
 };
 
 &i2c2 {
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/pyra-mainboard-v5.3.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/pyra-mainboard-v5.3.dtsi
@@ -55,6 +55,19 @@
 	compatible = "nxp,pcal6524";
 	interrupt-parent = <&gpio6>;
 	interrupts = <1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;	/* gpio6_161 */
+
+	/*
+	 * The TS3A227E's interrupt (P16). It reaches the kernel configured
+	 * as an output, so gpiolib refuses it as an IRQ and the jack
+	 * detector fails to probe with -EIO. Make it an input before
+	 * anything asks for it.
+	 */
+	mic-int-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <14 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		input;
+		line-name = "mic-int";
+	};
 };
 
 &i2c2 {
